# ---- local gate slots (bin/gate.sh --local) ----------------------------------
# bin/gate.sh runs a tree's gate on the shared Fly test host by default. With
# --local it runs the tree's bin/run-tests-in-docker.sh on this machine, and at
# most GATE_LOCAL_SLOTS of those run at once. The next one prints one line and
# waits for a slot. Ctrl-C ends the wait.
#
# Default 2, range 1..6. A value outside that range is exit 2, not a clamp.
# On 2026-10-14 a Mac ran 7 local test containers, each with `xargs -P 6`, on
# 18 cores: load 167. Two keeps a Mac usable. This is a per-machine value in
# the shell env; no settings row sets it.
#GATE_LOCAL_SLOTS=2
